cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use quiver in your work, please cite it — and cite the papers it reimplements (see references)."
type: software
title: "quiver: real-time Eulerian video magnification and remote photoplethysmography in the browser"
abstract: "A motion microscope that runs in the browser. Amplifies invisible colour and motion changes in live video (blood flow in the face, breathing, vibration) with a WebGL2 reimplementation of Eulerian Video Magnification, and measures heart rate from skin colour with POS/CHROM remote PPG. On-device, no server."
authors:
